  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecclesial Panamazonian network - Brazil national commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project continues its assistance to the CNBB&#x2019;s Ecclesial Pan Amazonian Network (REPAM) in its support for indigenous peoples, rural communities and other groups who have been severely impacted by the advance of mining, large infrastructure projects and climate change in the Amazon region.  It aims to enhance the action of the Catholic Church in the region, through establishing a platform for exchange and collaboration which supports and articulates the efforts of the missionary religious congregations, dioceses and secular organisations working in defence of the Amazon forest, the local populations and the common good. 

It will achieve this through:

&#x2022;	definition of strategies, goals, procedures and a basic agenda and structure of work for the coming years;
&#x2022;	dissemination of REPAM mission, vision and values and objectives among the bishops, congregations, missionaries and CSOs in the Amazon region;
&#x2022;	training and other joint initiatives aiming to strengthening advocacy of the Catholic Church at local, national and international level in defence of the region and vulnerable populations.</narrative>
  </description>
